794167210423954106395800606094\"","\"price_date\"","\"share_date\"","\"market_cap_cr\"","\"FY26_reported_standalone_PAT_cr\"","\"reported_PE_diagnostic\"","\"normalized_PE\"","\"current_EV\"","\"current_EV_EBITDA\"","\"2026-10-14 stale secondary last trade\"","\"8.9467\"","\"11.90812612471637587043267349972615601283\"","\"Unreliable normalized profit, stale March cash/debt and intervening cash/claims movements; no supported current enterprise-value bridge.\"","\"conclusion\"","\"Three economically relevant named comparators, using a common FY25 structural/operating period available before 20 October 2026. Not an exhaustive peer audit, current valuation screen or investment ranking. Stronger/weaker describes the stated channel, scale or margin dimension, not overall investment quality.\"","\"source_id\"","\"primary_facts\"","\"comparison\"","\"limits\"","\"revenue_lakh\"","\"pat_lakh\"","\"pages\"","\"Sky Gold and Diamonds Limited\"","\"B2B supply to jewellery retailers/wholesalers; disclosed capacity of 1,050 kg/month. FY25 consolidated revenue was ₹354,801.96 lakh and PAT ₹13,265.53 lakh; acquisitions of Sparkling Chains and Starmangalsutra expanded the product mix.\"","\"Stronger disclosed industrial scale and product/customer access than Retaggio; its manufacturing-supplier model is economically closer than a pure branded retailer.\"","\"Consolidated acquisition scope differs from Retaggio standalone. Reported PAT margin 3.74% illustrates that scale and metal-pass-through revenue do not guarantee high margins. No valuation multiple is transferred.\"","\"354801.96\"","\"13265.53\"","\"RBZ Jewellers Limited\"","\"Integrated antique-gold manufacturing, wholesale/job work and Harit Zaveri retail. FY25 mix: wholesale 37% of revenue / 20% of volume; job work 2% / 50%; retail 61% / 30%. Revenue was ₹53,014.85 lakh and PAT before OCI ₹3,879.85 lakh.\"","\"Stronger disclosed direct-customer channel and mix visibility; the job-work volume/revenue disparity is a concrete warning against treating gross revenue as physical demand.\"","\"Retail integration and antique-gold specialization make its 7.32% PAT margin non-transferable to Retaggio. Not a like-for-like market-multiple or consolidated-margin comparison.\"","\"53014.85\"","\"3879.85\"","\"Moksh Ornaments Limited\"","\"FY25 Note 22 separates domestic goods of ₹47,641.35 lakh, export sales ₹10,324.50 lakh and services ₹24.35 lakh. Main P&L revenue of ₹57,990.20 lakh and PAT ₹842.76 lakh imply a 1.45% PAT margin.\"","\"A weaker-margin comparator than RBZ and Sky on the same reported FY25 measure, despite substantial gross sales. It tests the assumption that jewellery-supply scale necessarily produces pricing power.\"","\"Different product/export mix, financing and accounting basis. The board headline of ₹58,251.51 lakh differs from main P&L/Note 22, so those identified statement values are used, not a blended number. No full peer-quality clearance is claimed.\"","\"57990.20\"","\"842.76\"","\"Retaggio has not demonstrated the scale/channel advantages shown by the stronger comparators; weaker-margin evidence prevents assuming high sustainable margins from sector growth. Its unresolved own figures cannot establish superiority to any peer. No peer mean, current price, P/E or premium is used to set its valuation.\"","\"commitment\"","\"observed_outcome\"","\"assessment\"","\"22 March 2025 prospectus; 7 April 2025 listing\"","\"IPO net objects: ₹1,150 lakh working capital and ₹190 lakh debt repayment; gross issue 6,198,000 shares at ₹25.\"","\"Share issue/listing is corroborated in FY26 annual history. Deployment cannot be independently traced through a clean cash/premium bridge.\"","\"Share issuance delivered; economic deployment and cash returns unverified, not a completed-return success.\"","\"11 December 2025 approval; 13–22 January 2026 issues\"","\"19,110,000 warrants at ₹26, 25% upfront and 75% on optional exercise within 18 months.\"","\"March shares 18,168,160; 20 October 20,992,160. Signed 20 October notice confirms 504,000 new shares and ₹0.9828 crore received; 13,684,000 warrants remain.\"","\"Documented conversion milestones delivered; future ₹26.6838 crore is optional, not promised or committed cash.\"","\"15 April 2026 proposal; 23 April 2026 incorporation reported subsequently\"","\"Proposed 76% investment in Lodha Heritage and transition of manufacturing/retail operations.\"","\"FY26 annual subsequent-event disclosure and Q1 consolidated review establish subsidiary existence. Original ownership/transition agreement and actual business transferred were not obtained.\"","\"Formation corroborated; 76% and business allocation remain explicitly qualified, no integration-success conclusion.\"","\"15 April 2026 postal proposal, effective 1 April 2026\"","\"MD annual salary proposed to rise from ₹24 lakh to ₹60 lakh, with additional perquisites capped at salary.\"","\"Retrieved notice states proposed terms; actual payments and final vote outcome not independently reconciled with the nil RPT table.\"","\"Proposal is not treated as actual remuneration paid or proven shareholder approval.\"","\"26 August 2026 board approval; 16 October 2026 agreement\"","\"Purchase 3,261.65 sq ft property for ₹10 crore plus actual transaction charges.\"","\"Signed agreement announcement is available; instalments, paid amount, funding, readiness and incremental output are not established.\"","\"Agreement milestone delivered; commissioning, funding and returns remain open rather than assumed on time.\"","\"FY26 controls assertions; 15 May 2026 audit\"","\"Board claims functioning audit trail and internal-audit arrangements.\"","\"Main audit/CARO contain contradictory audit-trail/internal-audit statements; separate IFC annexure also conflicts with exemption wording.\"","\"Control assertion is not independently validated; requires written reconciliation.\"","\"This is a dated promises-versus-observed-outcomes ledger, not an invented historic execution score.\"","\"review_date\"","\"information_cutoff_unchanged\"","\"model_assumptions_unchanged\"","\"factor_scores_and_gates_unchanged\"","\"section_review\"","\"update_log\"","\"quality_check\"","\"final_quality_checks\"","\"v 3.0, original supplied edition\"","\"2026-10-23\"","\"section\"","\"evidence\"","\"complete with explicit holds\"","\"Business, decisive collection/funding risk and conditional classification; compounder designation explicitly withheld.\"","\"complete\"","\"Exact issuer, cutoff, stale price, standalone/subsidiary scope, accounting inconsistency, five-year horizon, 15% equity hurdle, separately 14% WACC,₹5 lakh reference and gates.\"","\"13 factors, exact Decimal contributions, missing-data bounds, caps, confidence, sensitivity and no ranking.\"","\"complete with declared gaps\"","\"Product/manufacturing-trading mix, customers, physical scale, domestic scope, subsidiary; reliable current volumes and mix remain ND.\"","\"Three named primary-sourced economic peers; explicit stronger scale/channel and weaker-margin dimensions and comparability limits; no invented peer valuation.\"","6","\"complete with NS organic growth\"","\"Exact endpoints/intervals, annual rupee additions and nominal CAGRs; partial takeover and pass-through caveats; current comparable quarter.\"","7","\"complete with NS capital returns\"","\"Accessible demand/capacity and property funding constraints; capital definition and incremental-return limitations, GQS cap.\"","\"complete with unresolved outcomes\"","\"Dated commitment-versus-outcome table, RPT/remuneration/tax/title/control evidence; no abuse inference beyond evidence.\"","9","\"complete with explicit unavailable metrics\"","\"Original/restated/comparative statements; CFO ratio-of-sums, capex, operating/financing classifications, capital bridges and dilution. Reliable normalized PAT/average-capital ROIC/ROCE/ROE and lease quantification remain NS/ND with reasons.\"","\"complete but unsupported fair value\"","\"Current-share diagnostic P/E; current EV/normalized multiples explicitly NS; cash model, finite optional rescue, earned terminal, reverse trials, sensitivities and hurdle prices.\"","11","\"Strongest counterargument, collection-driven funding failure, structural impairment risk and conditional recovery limitations.\"","12","\"complete; speculative/unsupported\"","\"Dilution-aware 5x/10x earnings/revenue arithmetic and linked model-domain test, without extrapolation or success probabilities.\"","\"Seven company-specific monitoring rows with baselines, milestones, warning and thesis-break thresholds and review events; no automation created.\"","14","\"Hold override precedes matrix; research/evidence-repair priority, not eligible purchase or compounder; price alone cannot clear gates.\"","\"Source URLs/pages/hashes, assumptions, open questions, change log and standalone reconstruction.\"","\"change\"","\"factor_change\"","\"gate_change\"","\"model_change\"","\"thesis_impact\"","\"supersedes\"","\"Added missing named peers and completed dated execution, current valuation, growth, monitoring and framework presentation checks.\"","\"None\"","\"No favorable classification; completeness repair only.\"","\"Initial backup version 0; same owned Library identities updated with version guards.\"","\"All 16 v3 final checklist items are explicitly mapped to report/source/model records; unavailable material evidence stays visible as NS/ND. Independent numeric/recovery review is separate evidence, not manufactured by this checklist.\"","\"item\"","\"topic\"","\"Identity and scope\"","\"checked; material evidence gaps remain explicitly disclosed\"","\"Sections 2 and 15, security_extract.json; exact issuer, standalone scope and source/price dates.\"","\"Primary evidence and assumptions\"","\"Sections 4–10 and 15; signed records retained as factual extracts, assumptions and secondary facts separately labelled.\"","\"Audit, RPT, financing and dilution\"","\"Sections 8–10, audit_evidence.json and security_extract.json; four proportionate Hold gates.\"","\"Periods and units\"","\"Sections 2, 6 and 9; all original/restated/comparative vintages retained; no invented quarterly cash-flow statement.\"","\"Real versus nominal growth\"","\"Sections 6–7; takeover, metal pass-through and mix separate from nominal growth; organic growth NS.\"","\"Cash conversion and capex\"","\"Section 9 and financial_calculations.json; CFO/PAT uses sums, cash capex and property separately deducted.\"","\"Incremental capital returns\"","\"Sections 7 and 9; numerator, financing-capital proxy, timing and comparability caveats; economic incremental ROIC NS.\"","\"Valuation accounting consistency\"","\"Sections 9–10; normalized earnings and lease completeness NS/ND, explicit taxes, shares, warrants, minority and debt.\"","\"Cash and funding coherence\"","\"Section 10 and model_output.json; 221 complete or first-breach-stopped paths, bounded optional funding and earned continuation.\"","\"Canonical factors and weights\"","\"Section 3 and score_audit.json; same 13 factors, each applicable aggregate has total weight 100%.\"","\"Missing evidence and confidence\"","\"Sections 2–3 and factor_evidence.json; exact NS, coverage and bounds, no reweighting.\"","\"Scores and overrides\"","\"Section 3 and verify_research.py; raw/final arithmetic, persistent cash cap, no unsupported governance/funding-fail override.\"","\"Classification and compounder criteria\"","\"Sections 1 and 14; Hold precludes favorable classification; compounder designation explicitly withheld.\"","\"Position-based liquidity\"","\"Sections 2 and 10, market_extract.json; ₹5 lakh reference, 3,000-share lot, stale quote and incomplete bars; exit capacity ND.\"","\"Bear case and thesis break\"","\"Sections 11 and 13; strongest counterargument, collection/funding impairment mechanism and event-specific warning thresholds.\"","16","\"Ranking and unfinished evidence\"","\"Sections 3 and 14; no score ranking or universe winner; unresolved evidence